{"type":"standard","title":"Lily Tang Williams","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Lily Tang Williams</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q130280879","titles":{"canonical":"Lily_Tang_Williams","normalized":"Lily Tang Williams","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Lily Tang Williams</span></span>"},"pageid":77843426,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Lily_Tang_Williams_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/330px-Lily_Tang_Williams_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":441},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/Lily_Tang_Williams_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2189,"height":2925},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1377069798","tid":"6f5048b5-baa8-11f1-a02c-9c8fe232bc92","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:20:01Z","description":"American perennial candidate (born 1964)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lily_Tang_Williams","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lily_Tang_Williams?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lily_Tang_Williams?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Lily_Tang_Williams"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lily_Tang_Williams","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Lily_Tang_Williams","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lily_Tang_Williams?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Lily_Tang_Williams"}},"extract":"Lily Tang Williams is an American activist, businesswoman, and perennial candidate who chaired the Colorado Libertarian Party from 2015 to 2016. She unsuccessfully ran for the U.S. House of Representatives in New Hampshire's 2nd congressional district as a Republican in 2022 and 2024, losing the Republican primary in 2022 and losing the general election as the Republican nominee to Maggie Goodlander in 2024. She was also the Libertarian nominee for the U.S. Senate in Colorado in 2016 and unsuccessfully ran for the Colorado House of Representatives as a Libertarian in 2014. She is again running for the U.S. House of Representatives in New Hampshire's 2nd congressional district in 2026.","extract_html":"<p><b>Lily Tang Williams</b> is an American activist, businesswoman, and perennial candidate who chaired the Colorado Libertarian Party from 2015 to 2016. She unsuccessfully ran for the U.S. House of Representatives in New Hampshire's 2nd congressional district as a Republican in 2022 and 2024, losing the Republican primary in 2022 and losing the general election as the Republican nominee to Maggie Goodlander in 2024. She was also the Libertarian nominee for the U.S. Senate in Colorado in 2016 and unsuccessfully ran for the Colorado House of Representatives as a Libertarian in 2014. She is again running for the U.S. House of Representatives in New Hampshire's 2nd congressional district in 2026.</p>"}